# Copy this file to `.env.local` (gitignored) and paste your key after the `=`.
#
# WITH NO KEY THIS APP STILL RUNS. `/api/chat` streams the builder's own mocked
# turn — the kit's `createMockResponder()` for the words, plus a hand-framed
# `kai_artifact` tool call carrying a deterministically generated page — instead
# of calling a provider. The browser code is byte-for-byte the same in both
# modes; the seam is in server/chat.ts. So the only thing a key changes is who
# writes the page.
#
# UNPREFIXED on purpose. Vite only inlines VITE_-prefixed vars into client code,
# so this name can never end up in the browser bundle. There is no
# VITE_OPENROUTER_API_KEY and there must never be one.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Any chat model OpenRouter serves. OpenRouter normalises every model onto the
# OpenAI chat-completions shape, so `readOpenAIStream` parses all of them.
# Real mode asks for a WHOLE HTML document inside one tool call, so pick a model
# that is good at long structured output and give it room with the ceiling below.
#
# NOT the corpus default `anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5`. This app's reply IS a
# streamed tool call, and OpenRouter's streamed `tool_calls` argument deltas come
# back as invalid JSON on its Anthropic routes (a stray `}` near the end). The
# same request non-streamed parses fine and OpenAI's streamed deltas parse fine,
# so it is an upstream defect — but on an Anthropic model this app produces no
# page at all. Verified both ways; see README, "Real mode".
OPENROUTER_MODEL=openai/gpt-4o-mini

# Cost ceiling per reply. Higher than the other corpus apps' on purpose: a reply
# here carries an entire page, not a paragraph. Too low and the tool call is
# truncated mid-argument, the JSON never parses, and no version appears.
OPENROUTER_MAX_TOKENS=8000
